# Yojana Setu — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in values as needed.
# Currently the app requires NO environment variables to run:
# all scheme data, matching, and persistence are client-side.
#
# The only variable read by the build tooling is DISABLE_HMR,
# which is set by the AI Studio hosting environment (not by you).
# Leave it unset for normal local development.

# Supabase backend (optional — the app runs fully offline/local without these).
# When set, authentication becomes real (email/password + Google OAuth) and
# profile/scheme/tracker/document data syncs to the per-user cloud backend.
# Never commit real keys: copy this file to `.env` for local dev; in
# production set them in Vercel → Project Settings → Environment Variables.
# Only the ANON (publishable) key belongs here — never the service_role key.

# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key
